+From: Yang Siyuan <hsyysy@163.com>
+Subject: usb: phy: generic: request VBUS only if described
+
+Adapted for the MYIR Linux 6.12 build from the posted Linux USB patch:
+https://lore.kernel.org/linux-usb/20261026144800.1392738-1-hsyysy@163.com/
+The patch is a local backport of a proposal, not a claim of upstream merge.
+Do not substitute an imaginary fixed 5V regulator for an unknown Type-C path.
+
+--- a/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c
++++ b/drivers/usb/phy/phy-generic.c
+@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
+ #include <linux/clk.h>
+ #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
+ #include <linux/of.h>
++#include <linux/property.h>
+ #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+ #include <linux/delay.h>
+ 
+@@ -256,7 +257,10 @@ int usb_phy_gen_create_phy(struct device
+ 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(nop->vcc),
+ 				     "could not get vcc regulator\n");
+ 
